    given-names: "Keiji"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: "v0.3.1-integrated-revision-source-license-checked"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
url: "https://github.com/yokken0907/dynamical-threshold-theory-of-sleep"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yokken0907/dynamical-threshold-theory-of-sleep"
abstract: "Claim-bounded integrated model and audit synthesis for DTTS sleep-like recovery-transition toy networks. The release combines the original network-dynamical model, thresholded sleep-like gate, selective protection, reduced free-energy closure, and v0.2.0-v0.2.8 audit results covering hysteresis-like persistence, perturbation recovery, topology/noise robustness, failure boundaries, rescue-regime classification, and frozen holdout behavior. It does not claim clinical sleep diagnosis, medical advice, treatment guidance, human or animal sleep-data validation, EEG or wearable-device prediction, or a complete biological theory of sleep."
keywords:
  - DTTS
  - sleep-like recovery transition
  - adaptive networks
  - threshold dynamics
  - hysteresis
  - selective protection
  - rescue regimes
  - toy model
  - claim boundary
  - evidence-led protocol
